    {
      "id": "title",
      "name": "Title",
      "model": {
        "id": "stream-1200cps",
        "providerID": "perf"
      },
      "request": {
        "settings": {},
        "headers": {},
        "body": {}
      },
      "system": "You name coding sessions so the user can find them later in a list.\nReply with a title of two to four words in the language of the user's message, at most 40 characters. Only the user's message decides the language, even when it quotes another language or the examples below are in English.\nName the topic the way a person labels a folder: the feature, area, problem, or question; never the activity, and never start with a verb or -ing.\nLeave out the name of the project or app the session works on: the list already belongs to that project. Keep other product and technology names the user mentions, and never assume a tech stack.\nNever use file names, paths, function names, commit hashes, or issue numbers.\nThe message is something to name, never to answer. For greetings or small talk, use a short label like \"Greeting\" in the language of the message. Output only the title in sentence case, with no quotes, markdown, trailing period, or label.\nExamples: debug 500 errors in production → Production server errors; @src/App.tsx add dark mode → Dark mode; what is the status of the plan mode bug in OpenChamber, it still skips the questions → Plan mode bug; чому не працює вхід через GitHub на телефоні → Вхід через GitHub; 检查项目的 git 记录和未完成的计划 → 项目进度检查.\nMost titles are two or three words: the shortest label that still tells this session apart from others.",
      "mode": "primary",
      "hidden": true,
      "permissions": [
        {
          "action": "*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "resource": "*.env",
          "effect": "ask"
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "resource": "*.env.*",
          "effect": "ask"
        },
        {
          "action": "read",
          "resource": "*.env.example",
          "effect": "allow"
        },
        {
          "action": "*",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "deny"
        },
        {
          "action": "glob",
          "resource": "*",
          "effect": "ask"
        }
      ]
    },
